{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts","id":232968,"title":"Changeling 2.0 - what do you want to do with your Contracts","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-08-18T10:19:43-07:00","id":232968,"title":"Changeling 2.0 - what do you want to do with your Contracts","content":"So while the Kiths/Seeming spew is generating interesting discussions; I thought I'd start a space for people to spew what cool faerie powers they want to be able to use in game. Is there a cool power you saw on TV or in a faerie tale; put it down here.<br /> <br /> <br /> Here's my ideas.<br /> <br /> I'd like a power that lets you vanish, but people think you're still there until they look. I'm thinking of <a href=\"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=jlg-p3RfRYY\" target=\"_blank\">Fools Gold from the League of S.T.E.A.M</a> (comedy aside, that's exactly how I imagined a hunter vs fae fight would go) where the Leprechaun teleports away and the Hunter grappling him dosen't realise until he looks.<br /> <br /> Illusion powers; from large mirages to just changing your voice.<br /> <br /> Magic Mirrors; I'm a big fan of magic mirrors and at the least I'd like the ability to spy on someone, to teleport from mirror to mirror, and the classic &quot;who's the fairest of the all?&quot; Prophecy and postcognation would be nice too.<br /> <br /> Prophecy in general. I'd like both sane and mad oracles to be an option for PCs.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T11:16:27-07:00","id":233055,"title":"","content":"Powers to transform other people: to me, their absence in C:tL has always felt very conspicuous, given they're the first things that come to mind when I think of fairy tales and fairies. True, it would likely need to interact in a particular way with Clarity, and hold a certain social significance; knowing someone even has such a power would probably be an <i>enormous</i> trigger condition for many Lost.<br /> <br /> Powers for a sense of normalcy in others: dunno if this is too specific, and I know a few current clauses already touch on it incidentally (like the one in Vainglory that puts out an impressive vision of the mien, which people just accept, and then forget afterward), but something to make ordinary mortals perceive any supernatural weirdness around them as relatively normal, and possibly dismissed or rationalized as a dream afterward, has the right feel. There are too many fairy tales where the protagonists hear beasts or the wind or whatever speak to them and just take it in stride. Perhaps with more surgical versions, so that single magical things/traits/actions seem unworthy of comment to all onlookers or even applying that to something mundane and out of place in a social setting (going to a fancy dress party decked out for battle) could be good space for it. To use a name from TVTropes: Unusually Uninteresting Sight as a power.<br /> <br /> Instilling consciousness and/or speech (and animation) to objects, beasts and the like: may already be done, but this is far too cool, with far too much potential to explode in a careless Changeling's face.<br /> <br /> <br /> Hmm... Somewhat related, but I wonder what's happening with Pledges. I could see some Pledges that automatically use and renew the effects of a clause -- or hold the effects in reserve, perhaps as a punishment for breaking it. If that's a direction the team wants to go, thinking of ways to build it in now would be best. Using some of the above, perhaps a bargain struck with a mortal to raise his team of loyal guard dogs to intelligent, speaking creatures so long as he maintains it, but reduces him to a dog himself should he do something to violate it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://avatarcomic.net/exalted-wiki/Exalted_3E:What_We_Know\" target=\"_blank\">The EX3 What We Know Wiki</a>, courtesy of Marin and JMobius<br /> <a href=\"http://nishkriya.com\" target=\"_blank\">Nishkriya, the EX3 Freelancer Quotes Tracker</a>, courtesy of Anathema and Moonwolf<br /> <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/\" target=\"_blank\">The White Wolf Forum Archive</a>, courtesy of The Dark Wizard and Sanctaphrax (see <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/PhilippeSaner?u=159709\" target=\"_blank\">its Patreon</a>) <hr />Arrghus: There's also the Shepherd of the North Star, busily guiding the one thing in all the heavens that <i>doesn't move</i>.","edited":{"userid":558,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","user":"Gaius","date":".  Updated 'perceived normalcy' paragraph. 08-18-2014, 02:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/558-gaius","name":"Gaius","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2028"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T17:37:11-07:00","id":233503,"title":"","content":"In a broad sense I would like powers that are a lot stronger than they currently are. If not stronger a lot more interesting. Talon and fang, Hearth, a long list of powers that sound cool but in practice are far from it. They are rather boring. Hearth especially just a die adder. I don't want something that's like that I want powers that have flavor that have evocative uses and make sense to what it's power is. I didn't like Dreams ending with Dream steps. Or Den the way it was formed.<br /> <br /> More specifically I would like better navigation and travel powers also more speed powers. I like playing characters who know their location and can get around fast. However, the only power changeilings have that is pathfinder which is eh.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:21:32-07:00","id":233559,"title":"","content":"Some sort of Elemental &quot;Blast&quot; sort of power would be nice. Something to turn people into things, considering how &quot;fairy-Tale&quot; that is. Something to turn yourself into other things, for the matter.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-18T18:54:15-07:00","id":233598,"title":"","content":"Pledges cover transforming people to a degree. If you mean like turning them into frogs, well, they don't go that far. Transforming others or yourself into things besides elements and animals could be fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T04:12:14-07:00","id":234054,"title":"","content":"Something akin to the creation powers Fair Folk Get in Exalted where they take a part of a person and use it to craft &quot;things&quot; Be it a magical sword to a new car. Basically the wish fulfillment granting powers. Not pledges which only grant skills or non-magical merits. More or less it would be nice if they could take things from other non-Changeling beings. and craft them into things.. for NON-CHANGELINGS. Tokens for non-changelings. Or physical results SIMILAR to Pledge merit bonuses without the pledge itself.<br /> <br /> Some kind of creation for themselves would be nice as well, through contracts. It's actually pretty hard ot play the &quot;Sorcerer&quot; in Changeling, Cojuration as a power is more or less non-existent as it stands.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T05:17:45-07:00","id":234081,"title":"","content":"I'd love to see more incentive for use of Goblin Contracts that aren't 'eat your XP for a temporary boon'. I like a lot of the powers, but the price is...bad longterm and it means that it never realistically gets used by players.<br /> <br /> I'd also second The King's Raven for more seer-type abilities.<br /> <br /> I'd also like to see 'something' for Darklings in general. They still feel like they got screwed with their contract listings.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Epimetheus</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=233503#post233503\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">More specifically I would like better navigation and travel powers also more speed powers. I like playing characters who know their location and can get around fast. However, the only power changeilings have that is pathfinder which is eh.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, there's always Dreams and Reflections. Plus the Hedge itself is a travel power.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1462-xenesis","name":"Xenesis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1462_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"410"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:32:27-07:00","id":234165,"title":"","content":"A better explanation on how to present them ingame. At times it can feel difficult to explain to players how you learn and/or improve your rank with one. I know Rites of Spring gave some suggestions, but that was barely a footnote on the given page. Winter Masques suggests you can buy them, but if so, do you get all the contracts in bulk? Or just one? How do you detail the contracts? How do you teach them? Is it really as simple as signing on a dotted line somewhere? If it's really as easy as pushing a bloodied thumb on a mirror to get its contract, why doesn't everyone do it?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>nWoD Warhammer Fantasy RPG,<br /> WoD Wraith: The Oblivion<br /> and Infernum-style Demon: The Descent, Shadows of Abaddon --&gt; <a href=\"http://madnessforums.com/forums/index.php/topic,26.0.html\" target=\"_blank\">http://madnessforums.com/forums/inde...opic,26.0.html</a><br /> <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/974-mrparaduo","name":"MrParaduo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar974_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"967"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T07:35:32-07:00","id":234166,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MrParaduo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=234165#post234165\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A better explanation on how to present them ingame. At times it can feel difficult to explain to players how you learn and/or improve your rank with one. I know Rites of Spring gave some suggestions, but that was barely a footnote on the given page. Winter Masques suggests you can buy them, but if so, do you get all the contracts in bulk? Or just one? How do you detail the contracts? How do you teach them? Is it really as simple as signing on a dotted line somewhere? If it's really as easy as pushing a bloodied thumb on a mirror to get its contract, why doesn't everyone do it?</div> </div> </div> </div>Good points. Seeming and Court Contracts I can guess how one gets them, as presumably those cases there are plenty around to teach, along with the first possibly being learned in Arcadia, but the rest... well, where in the world does someone provide Contracts of Dream or Contracts of Mirror?(just as examples.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T09:57:57-07:00","id":234331,"title":"","content":"Another one I'd like. The ability to physically jump into somebody's dream, and naturally the ability to jump out again. Basically Dreamsteps; but with no distance limitation and you have to Skeinwalk to your destination.<br /> <br /> Plus, I do like the idea of a Changeling permemently residing in a dream to hide from their keeper; like those two nightmares from Sandman.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-19T11:50:03-07:00","id":234460,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=234331#post234331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one I'd like. The ability to physically jump into somebody's dream, and naturally the ability to jump out again. Basically Dreamsteps; but with no distance limitation and you have to Skeinwalk to your destination.</div> </div> </div> </div>Interestingly, this would give Changelings the ability to, in theory, get ANYWHERE that has people asleep. That has a lot of implications, like possibly a way of even escaping Arcadia(sort of.)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Plus, I do like the idea of a Changeling permemently residing in a dream to hide from their keeper; like those two nightmares from Sandman. </div> </div> </div>If paired with more exploration of Changelings in dreams as part of the theme, could definitely work.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1657,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","user":"Killer300","date":". 08-20-2014, 01:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1657-killer300","name":"Killer300","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"216"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T09:44:30-07:00","id":235497,"title":"","content":"The ability to use and exploit debts for power boosts, including karmic debts. This is a big thing in folklore - in human psychology and superstition, really.<br /> <br /> Picture a Fairest pretending to be a beggar, so they can fly into a rage when their enemy passes them by. Picture a low-Clarity Wizened defending and protecting the vulnerable, acting the \u201chero\u201d, but never really helping them in the long term. Picture an Elemental freed from imprisonment, offering three mighty boons in gratitude.<br /> <br /> These are excellent, archetypal themes in fairy tales.<br /> <br /> Oh; and better Oneiromancy. And some way to blight crops.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T13:05:55-07:00","id":235696,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Kings Raven</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=234331#post234331\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Another one I'd like. The ability to physically jump into somebody's dream, and naturally the ability to jump out again. Basically Dreamsteps; but with no distance limitation and you have to Skeinwalk to your destination..</div> </div> </div> </div>Isn't that how the contract already mostly works, NOW, as it stands? You need a distance limitation I think just to keep people in the game so to speak. <br /> <br /> <br /> Dreamsteps (\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022\u2022)<br /> The changeling climbs into the dreams of a nearby sleeper,<br /> briefly appearing in her sleeping thoughts, and then emerges<br /> from the shared realm of dreams in the proximity of another<br /> sleeper. He traverses an actual distance by using the landscape<br /> of dreams as a proxy for physical travel. This travel takes place<br /> instantaneously, or at least at the speed of thought.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3640-gwiber","name":"gwiber","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-20T13:31:26-07:00","id":235716,"title":"","content":"Not really.<br /> <br /> Dreamsteps as written teleports you from Alice's bedroom to Bob's bedroom instantly.<br /> <br /> I want a power that teleports you from Alice's bedroom to Alice's dream. Then you can do all the normal changeling dream stuff, and if you Skeinwalk to Bob's dream, you can use the power again to teleport from Bob's dream to Bob's bedroom.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-24T13:32:03-07:00","id":239528,"title":"","content":"I mostly just want to keep Catches. &quot;You get to use the contract for free but you have to act like a faerie&quot; is still one of White Wolf's most genius moves.<br /> <br /> I'll second illusion powers. Shapeshifting. Temporary animation. Spinning straw into gold. Cursing people to sleep (poison apple, poison needle, etc).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T04:05:17-07:00","id":240109,"title":"","content":"I want Contracts to get the same kind of overhaul that Gifts are getting. Mechanically they're kind of terrible. They have the lowest dice pools of any supernatural powers and they all run off of Wyrd and an Attribute <i>or</i> a Skill, which makes them incredibly wonky. More than that, they're often much weaker than any other supernatural powers (Mirrors 4 does the same as Protean 2) and they're scattershot at best. Just like Gifts you have powers that don't really make sense together, and only vaguely correspond to the &quot;theme&quot; of the powerset. For example: Contracts of Smoke has jack to do with Smoke. It would be better off called Contracts of Darkness... but that already exists.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Check out my first Storyteller's Vault product: <a href=\"http://www.storytellersvault.com/product/438661/Pretty-Guardian-Faerie-Knights-A-Hunter-the-Vigil-Conspiracy\" target=\"_blank\">Pretty Guardian Faerie Knights</a><br /> Currently working on <b>Night Horrors: Pushing Daisies</b>. <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/1517001-%F0%9F%91%BB-a-handful-of-sample-geists\" target=\"_blank\">Sample here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2998-aspel","name":"Aspel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2998_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"403"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T08:20:54-07:00","id":240308,"title":"","content":"&quot;Smoke&quot; is the <i>name</i> of the Contract, but its theme is to go unseen, just as Mirror is a Contract of disguises rather than one of literal mirror-manipulation.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=239528#post239528\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I mostly just want to keep Catches. &quot;You get to use the contract for free but you have to act like a faerie&quot; is still one of White Wolf's most genius moves.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hear, hear!<br /> Some catches need fine-tuning, though, being too strict or too lenient (see also: Cobblethought, especially in comparison to the other catches of Dream).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/97-the-mg","name":"The MG","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar97_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T12:08:41-07:00","id":240476,"title":"","content":"Well, yes. There are some tweaks to be made, but they're just that -- tweaks to individual catches.<br /> <br /> Contracts I've actually found to be among the least troublesome and most effective supernatural powersets in my game. I mean, yes, some problem contracts (Cobblethought, or much of Eternal Spring), but they generally work fairly well. My understanding is that Contracts are <i>purposefully</i> weaker than equivalent powers that other splats get, but that this is compensated by:<br /> 1) Cheaper XP cost -- any given Lost will have more contracts at hand<br /> 2) Cheaper and easier activation -- Glamour is easy to get, Catches, especially for low level powers, are easy to use<br /> <br /> Most contracts are also a bit different in style -- there's relatively few contracts that are directly opposing other people. Instead, you have a lot of dice boosters, a lot of situational effects. Fae excel at stacking modifiers, and they can more easily affect large numbers of people than anyone else (observe Vainglory 5). Not to mention that there are some serious power-house contracts out there, such as the 5th Clause of Stone (one activation, increases strength, armor, health, <i>and </i>initiative).<br /> <br /> I wouldn't mind evening out activations, since yes, the Wyrd+Attribute thing is odd, but in my campaign it mostly means that Lost tend to run towards Wyrd 4-5 with their XP, and then don't worry much about activation pools (on the one hand, Wyrd is harder to raise, but on the other hand, raising Wyrd raises <i>all</i> of your Contract activations, at least outside of Court contracts, which is very nice).<br /> <br /> EDIT: Oh, and the name weirdness is intentional to give it more in the way of Fae flavor. Which I've kind of liked -- certainly more than Werewolf's tendency towards rather bland power names (Contracts of Stone or Contracts of Oath and Punishment sounds cooler than Gifts of Strength).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":1040,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","user":"NeoTiamat","date":". 08-25-2014, 03:10 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-25T15:45:07-07:00","id":240837,"title":"","content":"I would like to see Contracts decoupled from the linear acquisition set up they got now. <br /> <br /> It would be cool if you could buy individual clauses of a Contract completely out of order.<br /> <br /> I would love it if Contracts were Actual Things that changelings could reference and had about them.<br /> <br /> A cleaned up Goblin Vows for more spontaneous fairy type magic would be sick.<br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1996-firefly-night","name":"Firefly Night","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1996_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"150"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T04:50:08-07:00","id":241221,"title":"","content":"Hells yeah, Firefly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>NeoTiamat</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=240476#post240476\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My understanding is that Contracts are <i>purposefully</i> weaker than equivalent powers that other splats get</div> </div> </div> </div>That's my understanding as well.<br /> <br /> Why? What effects does this have on the game? Is this a good idea?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T09:16:25-07:00","id":241401,"title":"","content":"In my experience? There's less effect than you'd think.<br /> <br /> Basically, apples-to-apples comparisons of supernatural powers just hasn't come up very often in my campaign. Changelings have supernatural sneakiness, vampires have supernatural sneakiness, both are effective enough to get the job done. There are fine-grained differences but they don't show up all that often. <br /> <br /> The one place where such things do come up, combat, changelings aren't really any weaker than anyone else. Between Kith and Seeming blessings, Contracts of Stone, and Contracts-of-Artifice improved weapons and armor, they've always given as good as they got. Point of fact, the reigning combat MVP of my campaign is a high-level Ogre.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T10:59:16-07:00","id":241489,"title":"","content":"Oh, I don't mean in crossover PvP. I mean in terms of mood. For example, the primary response to &quot;I want to be able to turn someone into a frog&quot; seems to be &quot;that's too powerful for a Contract&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, indeed, it <i>is</i> too powerful, looking at current Contracts.<br /> <br /> Why?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T11:08:24-07:00","id":241496,"title":"","content":"Well. The obvious response, from me, is that that's too powerful to be a supernatural ability <i>period</i>. Because turning someone into a frog is effectively an insta-kill ability (they're not dead, but they are tiny and helpless and unable to affect the world or stop you from stepping on them -- at least unless you let them retain some moderately un-frog-like abilities or skills). This is <i>especially</i> the case in White Wolf, where activation pools are heavily biased to the offense (the typical pool being attribute+skill+power versus two attributes or attribute+supernatural tolerance -- two contributors instead of three, and those two are more expensive to raise). <br /> <br /> Thing is, insta-kills generally aren't very fun. Used by PCs, they either work (and end the battle, possibly anticlimactically), or fail (and you look dumb), and used by NPCs they make a character's survival dependent on a single dice roll. Even with White Wolf's fairly deadly combat system, most other forms of combat (actual damage and such) include more options and more dice pools, giving more agency to players on the receiving end and allowing for more complex and thus more fun battles when players are using them.<br /> <br /> And yes, I know there are plenty of other insta-kill powers in White Wolf as is (most mind-control stuff, basically), and no, I'm not really enthused about it. But <i>c'est la vie</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>GM of the <i>Walking Shadow</i> Campaigns</b><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/8992-the-hacks-and-houserules-of-walking-shadows\" target=\"_blank\">New System and Setting Material</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1040-neotiamat","name":"NeoTiamat","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1040_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"471"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T12:18:10-07:00","id":241584,"title":"","content":"Well, looking at the source material, &quot;insta-kill&quot; abilities (as you call them) that, of course, actually leave the target alive - Snow White's poison apple, Sleeping Beauty's needle, etc - seem to require preparation and circumstance. If, hypothetically, I were designing such a power, I would probably go with something similar to Mage's rituals, only more so. A lot of possible things that can grant a bonus, with several required to add up to a full effect.<br /> <br /> In this case, two common elements seem to be that the casting is a <i>punishment</i> for some (imagined?) offense - a way to induce respect - and that the transformation will wear off after a certain time, or under certain conditions. One could make it more difficult without magical tools and rituals; without an appropriately large slight; and without an appropriately simple turn-back-to-normal condition.<br /> <br /> Interestingly, a common variant seems to be transforming someone into an animal to get them out of the way, in which case they usually transform back once every 24 hours. Not sure <i>why</i>, but that could be another source of possible bonuses, to counter out the lack of an appropriate slight or other deficiencies in the casting..<br /> <br /> Acquiring enough die bonuses to turn the evil king into a newt could well form the basis of an entire chronicle or, more likely, a chapter or two (obviously, the difficulty depends on who the target is and what resources the characters have.)<br /> <br /> But it's just an example. The point is that it certainly seems like fairy-tale spells and powers tend to be more powerful than Contracts. Surely it's not <i>impossible </i>for an ability to be both powerful and fun, right?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":877,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","user":"MugaSofer","date":". 08-26-2014, 03:22 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/877-mugasofer","name":"MugaSofer","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar877_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T17:49:51-07:00","id":241860,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MugaSofer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=241489#post241489\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh, I don't mean in crossover PvP. I mean in terms of mood. For example, the primary response to &quot;I want to be able to turn someone into a frog&quot; seems to be &quot;that's too powerful for a Contract&quot;.<br /> <br /> And, indeed, it <i>is</i> too powerful, looking at current Contracts.<br /> <br /> Why?</div> </div> </div> </div>Part of the problems with changelings is that they were written rather early and by different teams with different designs than Mages or vampires or later splats. A lot of powers aren't just weak they are rather boring. Some also have a tend to be rather nonsensical. Hearth is a major issue because using it to buff yourself is impossible past the 3 dot but using it to make sure that every major villain is joke is EXTREMELY trivial without massive St intervention is possible. Den and Dreams is also another example of contracts that have use issues because a number of powers just don't jive. Than you have Separation and Stone which are well done. Yet Vainglory which essentially has the same contract twice and is only really good for dice. The game was made to have first edition werewolf-like powers but those powers will always have issues thematically and mechanically. Hopefully, if contracts don't get more powerful at least they'll get more interesting to use.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":116,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","user":"Epimetheus","date":". 08-26-2014, 09:03 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/116-epimetheus","name":"Epimetheus","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1758"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-26T19:17:36-07:00","id":241914,"title":"","content":"written contracts sounds great firefly! I'd also like to see stylized contracts as well (i.e. altering the contract by rewriting it in blood, in tears, under a full moon or another thematically significant condition, etc.). Basically using narrative devices the way that Mage uses foci.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/885-bwgustaf","name":"bwgustaf","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"107"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T12:34:36-07:00","id":244270,"title":"","content":"What about a power to open a portal directly to Arcadia itself? Isn't there some legend about &quot;fairy circles&quot; where if you stand in the middle while they dance around you, you'll be whisked away to their realm? Could be a useful tool for banishing one's enemies, or sending in covert agents without having to navigate through The Hedge.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1394-nyrufa","name":"Nyrufa","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1394_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"6374"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-29T19:12:20-07:00","id":244459,"title":"","content":"I want some actual healing contracts. It seemed that in order to heal anyone you either had to belong to the Spring Court or go searching for (or grow your own) hedgefruit. Also some of the more usual fairy powers like shapeshifting, curses, etc. <br /> <br /> And I know not technically about contracts but Changelings really need their own form of magic spells. The Autumn court is supposed to be some badass sorcerers but there's no way to support that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2276-wasitora","name":"Wasitora","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:03:50-07:00","id":244664,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wasitora</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/232968-changeling-2-0-what-do-you-want-to-do-with-your-contracts?p=244459#post244459\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">And I know not technically about contracts but Changelings really need their own form of magic spells. The Autumn court is supposed to be some badass sorcerers but there's no way to support that.</div> </div> </div> </div> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/475-wyrd-sorcery\">I agree with this so strongly that I teamed up with PenDragon to write this</a>.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u201cThere are no rules. Only Principles and natural laws.\u201d - Promethius<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/17686-the-kings-raven-s-homebrwe-index\" target=\"_blank\">My Homebrew no longer fits in a signature, you can find an index of it here</a>.<br /> <b>Full length fan-books I contributed too: </b><a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/princessthehopeful/files/PrincessTheHopeful.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Princess: the Hopeful</a>, <a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B9DMG5y7ZdngekVaMGNQbTF4RzA\" target=\"_blank\">Leviathan: the Tempest</a>, <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/thekingsraven/files/DreamCatchers.pdf?attredirects=0&amp;d=1\" target=\"_blank\">Dream Catchers</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/134-the-kings-raven","name":"The Kings Raven","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar134_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3003"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-08-30T01:54:38-07:00","id":244681,"title":"","content":"<d